Error [E0204]: `values` is already shared in this call, so it can't be changed here too
  --> move_lambda_capture_identity_matches_rust_2021_places_6.jet:6:30
    |
  6 |     both(() -> first.len(), &values)
    |                              ^^^^^^
 Why: While something is being looked at, nobody else may be changing it
 Fix: Drop the extra use of `values`, or copy first with `~values`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0204

Error [E0212]: `values` cannot be passed with write access while `first` is still looking into it
  --> move_lambda_capture_identity_matches_rust_2021_places_6.jet:6:30
    |
  6 |     both(() -> first.len(), &values)
    |                              ^^^^^^
 Why: `first` is a live read view into `values[…]`; changing or moving the owner could invalidate that view
 Fix: Finish using `first` before changing `values`, narrow the view's scope, or make an owned copy
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0212
